			},
			"date": "2024-08-04T00:44:31.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> you’ll have a lot more control over this via Cloudfront. I am very pleased watching this thread. </p><p>Is that a weird thing to say? Am I being weird? Oh well.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112901010481644336",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/112901010481644336",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-08-04T00:51:43.881Z",
			"content": "<p>Worth noting that Netlify’s On-demand Builders provide global persistence across all edge nodes: <a href=\"https://www.netlify.com/blog/2021/10/25/faster-more-reliable-page-loads-with-update-to-on-demand-builders/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://www.</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">netlify.com/blog/2021/10/25/fa</span><span class=\"invisible\">ster-more-reliable-page-loads-with-update-to-on-demand-builders/</span></a></p><p>Alternatively, CloudFront has 13 Regional Edge Caches that (in my tests with a VPN) seem to be segmented too: <a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/cloudfront/features/?whats-new-cloudfront.sort-by=item.additionalFields.postDateTime&amp;whats-new-cloudfront.sort-order=desc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">aws.amazon.com/cloudfront/feat</span><span class=\"invisible\">ures/?whats-new-cloudfront.sort-by=item.additionalFields.postDateTime&amp;whats-new-cloudfront.sort-order=desc</span></a></p><p>CloudFront also offers an Origin Shield product that appears to provide a similar feature but I have not enabled it: <a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/cache-hit-ratio.html#cache-hit-ratio-use-origin-shield\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonClou</span><span class=\"invisible\">dFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/cache-hit-ratio.html#cache-hit-ratio-use-origin-shield</span></a></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
